# What JSON.parse() hands out nobody follows, so nobody knows what entries() above it gives. new Map() asks all that can be reached from it, and walks it as the language says: it calls @@iterator above it and then next(), and next() of array iterators is text of the library. No code of the program names next.
# sink(new Map(JSON.parse("[4,5,4]").entries()).size);
